Teach libxslt 1.1.32's ancient config.sub the Apple mobile triplets.

meta.yaml routes this file to version 1.1.32 -- the pin that goes with lxml 5.x
and libxml2 2.9.8 -- and everything newer to mobile-1.1.45.patch. This is the
original November 2024 lxml-enablement patch (PR #11), renamed when PR #48
introduced the version-suffixed layout.

build.sh configures with `--host=$HOST_TRIPLET`, and 1.1.32's config.sub is old
enough to know nothing about Apple's arm64/iOS naming, so it rejects the
triplet before configure gets started. This vintage of config.sub splits its
argument into a basic_machine plus an os beginning with `-`, so
`arm64-apple-ios` arrives as machine `arm64-apple` / os `-ios`, and
`x86_64-apple-ios-simulator` as machine `x86_64-apple-ios` / os `-simulator`.
The patch has one hunk for each half of that split:

  1. `arm64-apple | *-ios` joins the long list of accepted bare machine names,
     which completes the field with `-unknown` and leaves the os untouched.
  2. `-simulator` joins `-ios` in the accepted-os list.

The canonical triple this produces is not used for anything beyond parsing and
being different from the build machine's, which is what makes the build
register as a cross build; device-vs-simulator targeting comes from
CC/-isysroot, which forge sets. Without the patch no iOS slice configures.

How the siblings differ. mobile-1.1.45.patch, for modern libxslt, needs only an
`ios-simulator*` case in the `case $basic_os` block, because current config.sub
already handles `*-apple-ios` on its own. The same-era libxml2 patch,
recipes/flet-libxml2/patches/mobile-2.9.x.patch, reaches the same result with a
single case that forces `os=-none` so the os list never has to be edited, and
it carries an extra libxml2.syms hunk that has no counterpart here.

diff --git a/config.sub b/config.sub
index 7b334f9..a32642c 100755
--- a/config.sub
+++ b/config.sub
@@ -316,7 +316,8 @@ case $basic_machine in
 	| visium \
 	| we32k \
 	| x86 | xc16x | xstormy16 | xtensa \
-	| z8k | z80)
+	| z8k | z80 \
+	| arm64-apple | *-ios)
 		basic_machine=$basic_machine-unknown
 		;;
 	c54x)
@@ -1539,7 +1540,7 @@ case $os in
 		;;
 	-nacl*)
 		;;
-	-ios)
+	-ios | -simulator)
 		;;
 	-none)
 		;;
